IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- PENSION ADJUSTMENTS (regulations 78.3 and 78.4).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 801 to 821.
--
-- Both regulations are made "for the purposes of subsection 46(3.1) of the Act" (piece cp3) and give the
-- adjustment factor for a retirement pension that becomes payable before (78.3) or after (78.4) the month in
-- which the contributor reaches 65 years of age. A factor below 1 reduces the pension, a factor above 1 raises it.
--
-- "Reaches 65 years of age": section 2(2) of the Act applies, because neither regulation is among the
-- provisions section 2(2) excepts. The contributor is deemed to reach 65 at the beginning of the month AFTER the
-- month of the 65th birthday, so "the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age" is the month after
-- the birthday month (cpp-core-age.l4).
--
-- A month is the DATE of any day in it; the rules take the first day of it with `the month of a date`.

§ `Part V -- Pension Adjustments`

§§ `Regulation 78.3 -- a retirement pension that becomes payable before the month the contributor reaches 65`

-- src:801 | Pension Adjustments
-- src:802 | 78.3 For the purposes of subsection 46(3.1) of the Act, the adjustment factor for a retirement pension that becomes payable in a month before the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age shall be determined by the formula
-- src:803 | 1 – (A × B)
-- src:804 | where
-- src:805 | A is the number of months in the period beginning with the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable and ending with the month before the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age, or 60 months, whichever is less; and
-- src:806 | B is
-- src:807 | (a) 0.0050, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2010 and before January 1, 2012,
-- src:808 | (b) 0.0052, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2011 and before January 1, 2013,
-- src:809 | (c) 0.0054, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2012 and before January 1, 2014,
-- src:810 | (d) 0.0056, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2013 and before January 1, 2015,
-- src:811 | (e) 0.0058, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2014 and before January 1, 2016, and
-- src:812 | (f) 0.0060, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2015.
@ref Reg 78.3 (src:802)
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob MEANS
    `the month of a date`
        (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` dob 65)

@ref Reg 78.3 (src:802-805)
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 78.3 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month before the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob payable MEANS
    `the month of a date` payable LESS THAN (`reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob)

@ref Reg 78.3 (src:805)
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 78.3 — A, the number of months from the month the pension becomes payable to the month before the contributor reaches 65 years of age, or 60` dob payable MEANS
    min 60 (`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` payable (`reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob))

-- B is the monthly reduction rate, by the month in which the pension becomes payable. The text gives it for
-- months from January 2011 on; for an earlier month the text gives no figure, so the answer is NOTHING.
@ref Reg 78.3 (src:806-812)
GIVEN payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` payable MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2010 12 31) AND m LESS THAN (YMD 2012 1 1) THEN JUST 0.0050
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2011 12 31) AND m LESS THAN (YMD 2013 1 1) THEN JUST 0.0052
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2012 12 31) AND m LESS THAN (YMD 2014 1 1) THEN JUST 0.0054
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2013 12 31) AND m LESS THAN (YMD 2015 1 1) THEN JUST 0.0056
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2014 12 31) AND m LESS THAN (YMD 2016 1 1) THEN JUST 0.0058
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2015 12 31) THEN JUST 0.0060
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        m MEANS `the month of a date` payable

-- The factor is 1 - (A x B). NOTHING when the pension does not become payable before the month the contributor
-- reaches 65 (this regulation does not speak to it) or the month is one for which B is not given.
@ref Reg 78.3 (src:802-812)
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob payable MEANS
    IF `reg 78.3 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month before the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob payable
    THEN CONSIDER `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` payable
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (1 MINUS (a TIMES b))
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        a MEANS `reg 78.3 — A, the number of months from the month the pension becomes payable to the month before the contributor reaches 65 years of age, or 60` dob payable

§§ `Regulation 78.4 -- a retirement pension that becomes payable after the month the contributor reaches 65`

-- src:813 | 78.4 For the purposes of subsection 46(3.1) of the Act, the adjustment factor for a retirement pension that becomes payable in a month after the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age shall be determined by the formula
-- src:814 | 1 + (A × B)
-- src:815 | where
-- src:816 | A is the number of months in the period beginning with the month after the contributor reaches 65 years of age and ending with the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable, or 60 months, whichever is less; and
-- src:817 | B is
-- src:818 | (a) 0.0057, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2010 and before January 1, 2012,
-- src:819 | (b) 0.0064, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2011 and before January 1, 2013, and
-- src:820 | (c) 0.0070, if the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable is after December 31, 2012.
@ref Reg 78.4 (src:813-816)
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 78.4 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month after the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob payable MEANS
    `the month of a date` payable GREATER THAN (`reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob)

@ref Reg 78.4 (src:816)
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 78.4 — A, the number of months from the month after the contributor reaches 65 years of age to the month the pension becomes payable, or 60` dob payable MEANS
    min 60 (`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` (`reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob) payable)

-- B is the monthly increase rate. The text gives it for months from January 2011 on only.
@ref Reg 78.4 (src:817-820)
GIVEN payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` payable MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2010 12 31) AND m LESS THAN (YMD 2012 1 1) THEN JUST 0.0057
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2011 12 31) AND m LESS THAN (YMD 2013 1 1) THEN JUST 0.0064
        IF m GREATER THAN (YMD 2012 12 31) THEN JUST 0.0070
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        m MEANS `the month of a date` payable

@ref Reg 78.4 (src:813-820)
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob payable MEANS
    IF `reg 78.4 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month after the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` dob payable
    THEN CONSIDER `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` payable
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (1 PLUS (a TIMES b))
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        a MEANS `reg 78.4 — A, the number of months from the month after the contributor reaches 65 years of age to the month the pension becomes payable, or 60` dob payable
